# build artifact: dev.sh -b bundles the metasmith library in here for shipping.
# Generated, never edited; the source of truth is src/metasmith_libraries/.
src/fabfos/_library/

# Benchmark solve outputs and retrieved HPC results: multi-GB / 400 MB+ TSVs,
# reproducible from the recorded sockeye run key. The SCORE tables are small
# and ARE tracked.
transforms/build/benchmark/v3_build/run/
transforms/build/benchmark/v3_build/run_star_universe_baseline/

# The data-dependency library root. The bytes are DVC's job; git carries only the
# metasmith indexes, which are what a fresh checkout reads to know what the library
# is supposed to contain before any bytes exist.
#
# The directory re-include on the second line is load-bearing: git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so a bare `/data/*` + `!/data/_metadata` cannot reach
# an index nested under a tier -- the negation matches nothing and silently drops it.
# Written level by level rather than with `**`: a blanket `!/data/**/` re-include
# reaches nested checkouts too (data/validation/LASER is an upstream git repo), and
# `git add` turns an un-ignored directory holding a .git into a gitlink with no
# .gitmodules entry -- a broken submodule reference nobody asked for.
/data/*
!/data/*/
/data/*/*
!/data/_metadata/
!/data/*/_metadata/
